-Expert offloading starts from the distinction between sparse execution and full weight capacity~\cite{offloading,swapmoe}. Fiddler and DAOP choose CPU/GPU execution or movement; MoE-Lightning pipelines heterogeneous work; MoE-Infinity uses activation traces~\cite{fiddler,daop,lightning,moeinfinity}. ProMoE, Pre-gated MoE, Fate, and ExpertFlow provide lookahead, proactive caching, or token scheduling~\cite{promoe,pregated,fate,expertflow}. MECC's demand path instead consumes the original gate output and coordinates initial placement with online residency. The distinction concerns when information becomes available. A trace supplies a distribution before execution; a gate supplies the current demand during execution. MECC uses the former to initialize capacities and identities, and the latter to update membership. This lets the replacement mechanism remain responsive when the runtime stream differs from the calibration input.
