-HOBBIT and Specter use precision in expert loading; MoEpic divides experts into segments; SliceMoE caches precision slices; Mira combines staging with quantization~\cite{hobbit,specter,moepic,slicemoe,mira}. ZipMoE uses compression and affinity scheduling~\cite{zipmoe}. SSD-LLaMA, edge FlashMoE, and MoE-CORE address storage delivery, replacement, or coordinated residency~\cite{ssdllama,flashmoe,core}. MECC studies the interaction between an independent placement prior and online whole-expert retention across the two fast tiers under HDD-backed demand. This fixes the cached object as an unchanged FP16 expert. Segmenting an object or storing another precision can reduce the bytes required by one miss; retaining the whole object changes whether that miss occurs. The decisions can be complementary, but their performance effects arise from different mechanisms. We therefore keep representation and routing fixed when attributing the local retention benefit.
